WEBVTT

NOTE Prepared from local speech recognition and editorial correction; Chinese editorial translation. Century references express a preservation vision, not a guarantee.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000 line:10% size:90%
Tracing back to 1376, the Wu family lineage has survived through the sheer weight of ink and fragile paper.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.000 line:10% size:90%
But strokes of ink offer no sound, carrying cold dates and formal titles,

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.000 line:10% size:90%
while the human philosophy that built a bloodline fades completely into silence.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.000 line:10% size:90%
When the architects of a dynasty depart, their calculated risks, their private regrets,

5
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.280 line:10% size:90%
and the exact cadence of their voice disappear forever,

6
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.440 line:10% size:90%
stranding their descendants in quiet halls devoid of warmth.

7
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:38.600 line:10% size:90%
Today, the modern creators of family wealth stand on the precipice of that exact same erasure.

8
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:42.540 line:10% size:90%
A family portrait captured in 1962 begins to yellow,

9
00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:46.200 line:10% size:90%
its contrast fading as the physical chemistry breaks down.

10
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.560 line:10% size:90%
We are in the final countdown to capture the truth of this living generation,

11
00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.500 line:10% size:90%
because no future algorithm can resurrect a human voice it never heard,

12
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.500 line:10% size:90%
or deduce a memory that was never spoken.

13
00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.500 line:10% size:90%
And abandoning these fragile remnants in cardboard storage boxes

14
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:04.000 line:10% size:90%
or generic cloud folders does not save them.

15
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.500 line:10% size:90%
It merely delays their disappearance.

16
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.000 line:10% size:90%
A carved wooden seal, a tangled cassette tape of oral history,

17
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000 line:10% size:90%
and a folded letter from the old country,

18
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.140 line:10% size:90%
are scattered across disparate living rooms and continents.

19
00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:22.060 line:10% size:90%
Dragging them into a sterile online drive strips away their vital context,

20
00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:27.100 line:10% size:90%
creating a digital graveyard of unnamed files severed from the people they belong to.

21
00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:33.820 line:10% size:90%
True preservation demands securing the living spirit, the fierce ambition, and the heavy sacrifices

22
00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.660 line:10% size:90%
that defined a lifetime of choices.

23
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:42.260 line:10% size:90%
Protecting that essence requires an impenetrable foundation built to outlast us all.

24
00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:47.200 line:10% size:90%
We anchor these memories inside localized, century-grade optical cold storage.

25
00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:51.400 line:10% size:90%
By capturing the raw, uncompromised truth of your ancestors right now,

26
00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:57.100 line:10% size:90%
you guarantee their right to be understood and articulated by the intelligence engines of tomorrow.

27
00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.800 line:10% size:90%
The static archives of the past are preparing to speak,

28
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.600 line:10% size:90%
from a silent paper lineage to a living network,

29
00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:08.500 line:10% size:90%
from a fading portrait to a philosophy that speaks back.

30
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.100 line:10% size:90%
Will your bloodline survive the jump into the digital age?

31
00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:17.560 line:10% size:90%
Your data exists for a century. AI models will evolve for a century,

32
00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:19.300 line:10% size:90%
but your family endures for a century.

33
00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.000 line:10% size:90%
The window to save your founders is closing.

34
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.880 line:10% size:90%
Explore DeepFamily.

35
